      "publicId": "chal_coding_pdp_112",
      "name": "incremental-orders-extract",
      "type": "mini_coding",
      "title": "Extract orders incrementally with a watermark",
      "description": "The nightly copy of Rice Rocket's orders into the warehouse took two hours as a full extract. The editor holds `pipelines/orders_incremental.py` with its key blocks missing, each marked by a `# [ ]` line; some pieces are wrong on purpose. Fill every line so that `run_once` reads the watermark of the job `orders`, extracts every order changed at or after the watermark minus `lookback_minutes` (late commits must not be missed), upserts them into `fact_orders`, moves the watermark to the largest `updated_at` it actually read (never the clock; unchanged when nothing was read), and commits the load and the watermark together so a failed load saves neither. Run replays several nights on SQLite, including a late commit and a failed load, and compares the warehouse with the source.",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "outcomes": [
        "extract-load"
      ],
      "points": 30,
      "hints": [
        "Follow one late order: it commits after the extraction started, with an `updated_at` a few minutes before the watermark the run leaves behind. Which query of the next run still sees it, and which watermark makes that possible?",
        "Look at `datetime.strptime` and `timedelta` for the start of the window, `max(..., default=...)` for the new watermark, and `with wh:` in Python's sqlite3, which commits the whole block or rolls it back.",
        "A job that copies payments by `paid_at` might do: `start = last - timedelta(minutes=10)`, `rows = SELECT ... WHERE paid_at >= start ORDER BY paid_at`, `last = max([r.paid_at for r in rows], default=last)`, and inside one `with conn:` block both the upsert of the rows and `UPDATE job_state SET last = ?`."
      ],
      "coding": {
        "language": "python",
        "filePath": "pipelines/orders_incremental.py",
        "executionMode": "stdio",
        "timeLimitMs": 3000,
        "memoryLimitMb": 128,
        "scoringMode": "all_or_nothing",
        "maxAttempts": null
      },
